{"id": "EUVD-2026-98672", "enisaUuid": "af9c444e-f802-3954-a0ab-ad922ba85b64", "description": "Wazuh from 4.1.0 before 4.14.8 contains a missing origin check in wm_agent_upgrade that allows enrolled agents to issue upgrade_custom commands with attacker-controlled file_path. Attackers can inject an upgrade_custom message over the agent channel to read arbitrary files as root, exfiltrating /etc/shadow and client.keys.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T14:09:51", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/security/advisories/GHSA-r7hm-43xr-477j", "https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/releases/tag/v4.14.8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wazuh-4.1.0-before-4.14.8-arbitrary-file-read-via-upgrade-custom-command"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74034"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "41307063-b174-3b47-aa54-e26065363bc6", "product": {"name": "wazuh-manager", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}, "product_version": "4.1.0 <4.14.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "61bdca8a-5187-3cbe-9b5a-7ba83115bcab", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}], "isExploited": false}